#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classically simulating circuits with OBP for the latest version of Operator backpropagation (OBP)"
msgstr "Classical na pag-simulate ng mga circuit gamit ang OBP para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Operator backpropagation (OBP)"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classically simulating circuits with OBP"
msgstr "Classical na pag-simulate ng mga circuit gamit ang OBP"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/simulating-circuits-with-obp.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this guide, you will learn how to classically simulate `QuantumCircuit` instances to estimate expectation values entirely through the means of OBP.\n"
msgstr "Sa gabay na ito, malalaman mo kung paano i-simulate nang classical ang mga instance ng `QuantumCircuit` para tantiyahin ang mga expectation value nang buo sa pamamagitan ng OBP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since OBP will take an observable and backpropagate it through a given circuit, the \"simulation\" of a circuit amounts to computing the expectation value of the target observable with respect to this circuit.\n"
"As you will see later, the `qiskit-addon-obp` package is even capable of handling simple noise models, allowing you to compute noisy expectation values, too!\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil kukuha ang OBP ng isang observable at ibabackpropagate ito sa isang ibinigay na circuit, ang \"simulation\" ng isang circuit ay katumbas ng pagkalkula ng expectation value ng target na observable kaugnay ng circuit na ito.\n"
"Gaya ng makikita mo mamaya, kaya pa ng package na `qiskit-addon-obp` na humawak ng mga simpleng noise model, kaya makakalkula mo rin ang mga noisy na expectation value!\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Constructing an example circuit {#constructing-an-example-circuit}"
msgstr "Paggawa ng halimbawang circuit {#constructing-an-example-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the purposes of this guide, we will use the same example circuit as in the [Pauli term truncation guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms):\n"
msgstr "Para sa layunin ng gabay na ito, gagamitin natin ang parehong halimbawang circuit tulad ng sa [gabay sa Pauli term truncation](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, the above is purely the circuit describing the time evolution under a chosen Hamiltonian.\n"
"We also need an initial state to start from, with respect to which we compute the expectation values of our observable.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gayunpaman, ang nasa itaas ay purong circuit lang na naglalarawan ng time evolution sa ilalim ng napiling Hamiltonian.\n"
"Kailangan din natin ng initial state na panimulan, na gagamitin natin sa pagkalkula ng mga expectation value ng ating observable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Of course, we could choose the all-zero (or vacuum) state as our initial state, but to show how one would insert their own initial state, we choose a different one below.\n"
msgstr "Siyempre, maaari nating piliin ang all-zero (o vacuum) state bilang initial state, pero para ipakita kung paano maglalagay ng sariling initial state, pipili tayo ng iba sa ibaba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One possibility, would be to prepend the initial state to our time-evolution circuit above: `circuit.compose(initial_state, front=True)`.\n"
"But since we have already sliced our `circuit`, it is easier to simply insert the initial state as the first slice, which we do below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isang posibilidad ay i-prepend ang initial state sa time-evolution circuit natin sa itaas: `circuit.compose(initial_state, front=True)`.\n"
"Pero dahil hinati na natin ang ating `circuit` sa mga slice, mas madaling ilagay na lang ang initial state bilang unang slice, na gagawin natin sa ibaba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this way, we can simply replace the first slice with another initial state, if we want to exchange that in the future, without having to recompute our slices.\n"
msgstr "Sa ganitong paraan, madali nating mapapalitan ang unang slice ng ibang initial state kung gusto nating palitan ito sa hinaharap, nang hindi na kailangang kalkulahing muli ang ating mga slice.\n"

