msgid "As a sanity check (and to prove that this works) we can compare our result against Qiskit's `Statevector`:\n"
msgstr "Bilang sanity check (at para patunayang gumagana ito), maaari nating ihambing ang resulta natin sa `Statevector` ng Qiskit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some notes on performance {#some-notes-on-performance}"
msgstr "Ilang tala tungkol sa performance {#some-notes-on-performance}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The computational efficiency of the `backpropagate` call above will heavily depend on many things, including:\n"
"- the structure of the `circuit`\n"
"- the method of slicing the circuit\n"
"- the target observable\n"
"- the truncation parameters\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang computational efficiency ng tawag sa `backpropagate` sa itaas ay malaki ang nakasalalay sa maraming bagay, kabilang ang:\n"
"- ang istruktura ng `circuit`\n"
"- ang paraan ng paghiwa sa circuit\n"
"- ang target na observable\n"
"- ang mga truncation parameter\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since the `backpropagate` method simplifies the observable after every _slice_ has been applied, the number of gates in a slice can dramatically influence the computational burden.\n"
"The most aggressive strategy in terms of operator simplification can be achieved by slicing your circuit into slices of individual gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil pinapasimple ng method na `backpropagate` ang observable pagkatapos ma-apply ang bawat _slice_, malaki ang maaaring maging epekto ng bilang ng mga gate sa isang slice sa computational burden.\n"
"Ang pinaka-agresibong estratehiya sa pagpapasimple ng operator ay makakamit sa paghiwa ng circuit mo sa mga slice na may tig-isang gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Additionally, you can leverage all of the truncation mechanism built into the `backpropagate` method.\n"
"We did not do so above, effectively resulting in an exact expectation value, but you can learn how to in the [Pauli term truncation guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms).\n"
msgstr ""
"Bukod pa rito, magagamit mo ang lahat ng truncation mechanism na built-in sa method na `backpropagate`.\n"
"Hindi natin ito ginawa sa itaas, kaya eksaktong expectation value ang naging resulta, pero malalaman mo kung paano sa [gabay sa Pauli term truncation](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulating a noisy expectation value {#simulating-a-noisy-expectation-value}"
msgstr "Pag-simulate ng noisy na expectation value {#simulating-a-noisy-expectation-value}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `qiskit-addon-obp` package also supports handling of noise models in the form of `PauliLindbladError`s.\n"
"This is especially useful when you have characterized the noise model of the 2-qubit layers in your circuit, for example using the [`NoiseLearner`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/noise-learner-noise-learner).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sinusuportahan din ng package na `qiskit-addon-obp` ang paghawak ng mga noise model sa anyo ng `PauliLindbladError`.\n"
"Lalo itong kapaki-pakinabang kapag na-characterize mo na ang noise model ng mga 2-qubit layer sa circuit mo, halimbawa gamit ang [`NoiseLearner`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/noise-learner-noise-learner).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this section, you will see how you can use the `LayerError` objects returned by the `NoiseLearner` to compute noisy expectation values using OBP.\n"
msgstr "Sa seksyong ito, makikita mo kung paano magagamit ang mga object na `LayerError` na ibinabalik ng `NoiseLearner` para kalkulahin ang mga noisy na expectation value gamit ang OBP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Obtaining a noise model {#obtaining-a-noise-model}"
msgstr "Pagkuha ng noise model {#obtaining-a-noise-model}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally, you would execute the `NoiseLearner` to obtain a noise model of your specific circuit.\n"
"To avoid complexity (and randomness) in this tutorial, we will refrain from doing so, and instead hard-code some noise model for our circuit below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Karaniwan, ie-execute mo ang `NoiseLearner` para makuha ang noise model ng iyong partikular na circuit.\n"
"Para maiwasan ang komplikasyon (at randomness) sa tutorial na ito, hindi natin ito gagawin, at sa halip ay maghahard-code tayo ng ilang noise model para sa ating circuit sa ibaba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, we make sure that the structure of our data matches that of the [`NoiseLearnerResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-noise-learner-result).\n"
"In its current (non-transpiled) form, our circuit contains 4 unique layers of 2-qubit gates:\n"
"- `slices[1]`: which has `Rxx` gates acting on all odd pairs of qubits\n"
"- `slices[2]`: which has `Rxx` gates acting on all even pairs of qubits\n"
"- `slices[3]`: which has `Ryy` gates acting on all odd pairs of qubits\n"
"- `slices[4]`: which has `Ryy` gates acting on all even pairs of qubits\n"
msgstr ""
"Gayunpaman, tinitiyak natin na ang istruktura ng ating data ay tumutugma sa [`NoiseLearnerResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-noise-learner-result).\n"
"Sa kasalukuyang (hindi pa na-transpile) anyo nito, ang circuit natin ay may 4 na natatanging layer ng 2-qubit gate:\n"
"- `slices[1]`: na may mga gate na `Rxx` na kumikilos sa lahat ng odd na pares ng qubit\n"
"- `slices[2]`: na may mga gate na `Rxx` na kumikilos sa lahat ng even na pares ng qubit\n"
"- `slices[3]`: na may mga gate na `Ryy` na kumikilos sa lahat ng odd na pares ng qubit\n"
"- `slices[4]`: na may mga gate na `Ryy` na kumikilos sa lahat ng even na pares ng qubit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the cell below, we manually construct 4 `LayerError` instances for each one of these layers with some randomized error rates.\n"
msgstr "Sa cell sa ibaba, manu-mano tayong gumagawa ng 4 na instance ng `LayerError` para sa bawat isa sa mga layer na ito na may ilang randomized na error rate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you would have used the `NoiseLearner` to identify the unique 2-qubit gate layers of your circuit and characterize their noise, you would obtain a `NoiseLearnerResult` object.\n"
"This result would contain a list of `LayerError` objects, just like the ones we have manually constructed above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ginamit mo ang `NoiseLearner` para tukuyin ang mga natatanging 2-qubit gate layer ng circuit mo at i-characterize ang noise ng mga ito, makakakuha ka ng object na `NoiseLearnerResult`.\n"
"Magtataglay ang resultang ito ng listahan ng mga object na `LayerError`, katulad ng mga manu-mano nating ginawa sa itaas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each unique 2-qubit layer, the `LayerError` contains:\n"
"- the `QuantumCircuit` representing that 2-qubit gate layer\n"
"- the qubit indices which this circuit is acting upon\n"
"- the `PauliLindbladError` which represents the characterized noise model of this layer\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa bawat natatanging 2-qubit layer, ang `LayerError` ay naglalaman ng:\n"
"- ang `QuantumCircuit` na kumakatawan sa 2-qubit gate layer na iyon\n"
"- ang mga qubit index na pinagkikilusan ng circuit na ito\n"
"- ang `PauliLindbladError` na kumakatawan sa na-characterize na noise model ng layer na ito\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `PauliLindbladError` will contain two objects:\n"
"- the list of Pauli errors that have been characterized\n"
"- the error rates corresponding to each one of those Pauli errors\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang `PauliLindbladError` ay maglalaman ng dalawang object:\n"
"- ang listahan ng mga Pauli error na na-characterize\n"
"- ang mga error rate na tumutugma sa bawat isa sa mga Pauli error na iyon\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normally, the list of Pauli errors will be sparse. More specifically, it will contain the single-qubit Pauli errors on all qubits that have gates acting upon them as well as the two-qubit Pauli errors on all those qubits that are connected.\n"
msgstr "Karaniwan, sparse ang listahan ng mga Pauli error. Mas tiyak, maglalaman ito ng mga single-qubit Pauli error sa lahat ng qubit na may mga gate na kumikilos sa kanila pati na ang mga two-qubit Pauli error sa lahat ng qubit na magkakonekta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inserting the noisy layers into our circuit {#inserting-the-noisy-layers-into-our-circuit}"
msgstr "Paglalagay ng mga noisy na layer sa ating circuit {#inserting-the-noisy-layers-into-our-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous section, we have specifically constructed one `LayerError` for each of our known unique 2-qubit gate layers.\n"
"This means, we know which `LayerError` matches a specific one of our slices exactly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa nakaraang seksyon, partikular tayong gumawa ng isang `LayerError` para sa bawat isa sa ating mga kilalang natatanging 2-qubit gate layer.\n"
"Ang ibig sabihin nito, alam natin kung aling `LayerError` ang eksaktong tumutugma sa isang partikular na slice natin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Normally, when using the `LayerError`, you will need to figure out what the unique 2-qubit gate layer is, and where it occurs inside of your circuit.\n"
"You will then need to adjust your `circuit` and/or `slices` to insert the `LayerError` accordingly.\n"
"How to do this in the general case, is beyond the scope of this how-to guide.\n"
"**TODO: link to external documentation, once it exists!**\n"
"Here, our life is simpler because we know which slice a `LayerError` corresponds to.\n"
"Therefore, it is now just a matter of inserting new slices to represent the noise.\n"
msgstr ""
"Karaniwan, kapag ginagamit ang `LayerError`, kakailanganin mong alamin kung ano ang natatanging 2-qubit gate layer, at kung saan ito lumilitaw sa loob ng circuit mo.\n"
"Kakailanganin mo pang ayusin ang iyong `circuit` at/o `slices` para ilagay nang naaayon ang `LayerError`.\n"
"Ang kung paano ito gagawin sa pangkalahatang kaso ay lampas sa saklaw ng how-to guide na ito.\n"
"**TODO: link to external documentation, once it exists!**\n"
"Dito, mas simple ang buhay natin dahil alam natin kung aling slice ang tumutugma sa isang `LayerError`.\n"
"Kaya, usapin na lang ito ng paglalagay ng mga bagong slice para kumatawan sa noise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note, that we must wrap each `PauliLindbladError` from `LayerError.error` in a `PauliLindbladErrorInstruction` for it to be a valid `QuantumCircuit` instruction.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na kailangan nating i-wrap ang bawat `PauliLindbladError` mula sa `LayerError.error` sa isang `PauliLindbladErrorInstruction` para maging valid itong instruction ng `QuantumCircuit`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can check our work and draw the circuit below:\n"
msgstr "Maaari nating suriin ang ginawa natin at iguhit ang circuit sa ibaba:\n"

